tanding professional attainments and recognition in his or her specific field and renders a specified service to the University. Description of Primary Duties The Practitioner-in-Residence will: Provide direct patient care in the Missouri State University Physical Therapy Clinic, including both insurance-based and pro bono services. Serve as a clinical expert in oncologic physical therapy. Supervise and mentor Doctor of Physical Therapy ( DPT ) students in the provision of care within the pro bono clinic. Assist in the instruction and supervision of students in laboratory courses, contributing clinical expertise to support hands-on learning. Participate in department activities and initiatives as assigned by the Physical Therapy Program Director. Serve as a resource and role model for students and faculty in the application of evidence-based oncologic physical therapy. Engage in professional service or clinical scholarship Minimum Acceptable Qualifications The minimum acceptable qualifications for the position of Practitioner-in-Residence are prescribed in the Faculty Handbook. Additional Qualifications Additional required qualifications specific to this role include: Hold an active license as a physical therapist and be eligible for licensure in the state of Missouri. Hold a clinical doctorate in physical therapy ( DPT ). Hold a current, unrestricted license to practice physical therapy and be eligible for licensure in Missouri. Demonstrate effective written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrate the ability to establish and maintain positive working relationships with patients, students, faculty, staff, and community partners. Link to Job Description http://www.missouristate.edu/human/jobdescriptions/258421.htm Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date (If Close Date is blank then the posting is considered open until filled) Special Instructions to Applicants The first date of consideration is October 21, 2026, and review of applications will continue 