    "https://jobs.missouristate.edu/postings/88454": {
      "title": "Adjunct/Per Course Faculty, School of Teaching, Learning, and Developmental Science (Spring 2027)",
      "description": "Missouri State University Applicant Portal | Adjunct/Per Course Faculty, School of Teaching, Learning, and Developmental Science (Spring 2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Missouri State University Office of Human Resources Part-Time Staff Positions Adjunct/Per Course Faculty, School of Teaching, Learning, and Developmental Science (Spring 2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Missouri State University accepts applications for Adjunct Faculty to establish a pool of available candidates. By submitting an application for this posting you are applying to be a part of Missouri State University’s Adjunct Faculty pool for a potential course that may be offered in the applicable semester. There may not be a current opening. Applications and transcripts are evaluated prior to the selection of interviewees. To receive full consideration, include all documents requested by the department. Please attach an updated, detailed Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial transcripts can be attached as an optional document to the online application. Official transcripts may be required at time of hire to comply with reporting requirements for Missouri Law. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct/Per Course Faculty, School of Teaching, Learning, and Developmental Science (Spring 2027) Work Location Springfield Campus Out-of-State Employment Out-of-state employment is limited to Arkansas, Virginia, Maryland, and Washington, D.C., and subject to supervisor approval. Department School of Teaching, Learning & Developmental Sciences Sponsorship Information Applicants must be currently authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States on a full-time basis. This position is not eligible for work visa sponsorship. Term Spring Semester (per course faculty only) Begin Date -Spring Term 01/11/2027 Begin Date - Summer Term Begin Date - Fall Term Maximum credit hours Per Course faculty can teach 12 Credit Hours per 12 Month Period - Springfield Campus Description of Primary Duties Adjunct faculty teach by way of one of the following: 1) face-to-face on the Springfield campus, 2) face-to-face on a campus other than Springfield, 3) online, or 4) in a blended format that may include ITV or online teaching. Per course faculty are responsible for fulfilling all teaching expectations and must collect and provide data from courses to support program reviews. Per course faculty must communicate with students, faculty and administration associated with the course and program. Per course faculty represent MSU and its programs with professionalism and academic integrity. Minimum Acceptable Qualifications Adjunct faculty should possess a master’s degree or the equivalent professional experience in a field determined acceptable by the Dean. Additional Qualifications Adjunct faculty in Child Life Education must have a minimum of three years experience working in a child life program in health care facility, and they must hold current certification as a Child Life Specialist or hold certification by the appointment date. Adjunct faculty in Elementary education and Early Childhood Education, a minimum of three years teaching experience and certification are preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants Missouri State University accepts applications for Adjunct Faculty to establish a pool of available candidates. By submitting an application for this posting you are applying to be a part of Missouri State University’s Adjunct Faculty pool for a potential course that may be offered in the applicable semester. There may not be a current opening. Applications and transcripts are evaluated prior to the selection of interviewees. To receive full consideration, include all documents requested by the department. Please attach an updated, detailed Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial transcripts can be attached as an