    "https://jobs.missouristate.edu/postings/88148": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Social Studies and/or History Education) - 9 month appointment",
      "description": "Missouri State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor (Social Studies and/or History Education) - 9 month appointment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Missouri State University Office of Human Resources Part-Time Staff Positions Assistant Professor (Social Studies and/or History Education) - 9 month appointment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The first date of consideration is October 22, 2026, with the position remaining open until filled. To apply, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vita, unofficial transcripts, three confidential letters of recommendation and two syllabi: 1) a U.S. or World History survey and 2) a social studies methods or an upper-level History course. All application material, including letters of recommendation, must be submitted electronically to https://jobs.missouristate.edu/postings/87959 . Official transcripts required at time of hire. Employment will require a criminal background check at University expense. Missouri State is an equal opportunity employer and institution. Questions should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Michelle Morgan at MichelleMorgan@MissouriState.edu . Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor (Social Studies and/or History Education) - 9 month appointment Work Location Springfield Campus Out-of-State Employment Out-of-state employment is limited to Arkansas, Virginia, Maryland, and Washington, D.C., and subject to supervisor approval. Department History HR Home Department 020613 HISTORY Pay Grade Unclassified Sponsorship Information Applicants must be currently authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States on a full-time basis. This position may not be eligible for work visa sponsorship. Position only available to current, regular, full-time Missouri State University employees? No, Position is available to all applicants. Faculty Appointment Type Tenure Track Term (if applicable) 9 month Begin Date of Appointment 08/01/2027 Exempt/Non-Exempt Exempt General Function The Assistant Professor is a member of the ranked faculty with an intermediate academic rank who has demonstrated achievement in the areas of teaching, research, and professional service appropriate to the discipline. The Assistant Professor’s teaching responsibilities are assigned by the academic department head and may include serving as an academic advisor. The Assistant Professor engages in scholarly activities beyond those associated with teaching and is expected to demonstrate professional productivity in research, based upon the availability of resources and consistent with the mission of the University. Description of Primary Duties The successful candidate will be one of three faculty in the department whose primary responsibilities include providing courses in Secondary Social Science methods, supervising pre-service teachers, and other administrative duties as related to education accreditation and advising. Candidates must be prepared to serve as the Director of the BSED program. Additional undergraduate and graduate course offerings will depend upon the successful candidate’s area of specialization in history and/or area studies. Candidates must have relevant teaching experience in a secondary classroom and Ph.D. in History or History/Social Studies Education or related field. Minimum Acceptable Qualifications The minimum acceptable qualifications for the position of Assistant Professor are prescribed in the Faculty Handbook. Additional Qualifications The successful candidate will conduct and publish original research in their field and do appropriate departmental and university service. Link to Job Description http://www.missouristate.edu/human/jobdescriptions/21377.htm Open Date 09/14/2026 Close Date (If Close Date is blank then the posting is considered open until filled) 