      "description": "Missouri State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor (Political Science - American Political Behavior) - 9 mo. appt Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Missouri State University Office of Human Resources Part-Time Staff Positions Assistant Professor (Political Science - American Political Behavior) - 9 mo. appt Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The first date of consideration is October 12, 2026, and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Please provide the name, email address, and telephone number of at least three references who are familiar with your current work, especially your research, in the designated fields on the application form. If you have taught your own courses, please upload up to two syllabi in the “Course Documents 1 and 2” fields and up to two sets of student evaluations in the “Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness 1 and 2” fields. For additional information, contact: Dr. Gabriel Ondetti, Interim Head Department of Political Science and Philosophy Missouri State University gabrielondetti@missouristate.edu Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor (Political Science - American Political Behavior) - 9 mo. appt Work Location Springfield Campus Out-of-State Employment Out-of-state employment is limited to Arkansas, Virginia, Maryland, and Washington, D.C., and subject to supervisor approval. Department Political Science and Philosophy HR Home Department 020615 POLITICAL SCIENCE & PHILOSOPHY Pay Grade Unclassified Sponsorship Information Applicants must be currently authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States on a full-time basis. This position may not be eligible for work visa sponsorship. Position only available to current, regular, full-time Missouri State University employees? No, Position is available to all applicants. Faculty Appointment Type Tenure Track Term (if applicable) 9 month Begin Date of Appointment 08/01/2027 Exempt/Non-Exempt Exempt General Function The Assistant Professor is a member of the ranked faculty with an intermediate academic rank who has demonstrated achievement in the areas of teaching, research, and professional service appropriate to the discipline. The Assistant Professor’s teaching responsibilities are assigned by the academic department head and may include serving as an academic advisor. The Assistant Professor engages in scholarly activities beyond those associated with teaching and is expected to demonstrate professional productivity in research, based upon the availability of resources and consistent with the mission of the University. Description of Primary Duties The faculty member who holds this position will teach, conduct and publish research, and contribute to service activities. They will generally be expected to teach Quantitative Methods; American Political Behavior; Political Parties, Elections and Interest Groups; and American Democracy and Citizenship. Minimum Acceptable Qualifications The minimum acceptable qualifications for the position of Assistant Professor are prescribed in the Faculty Handbook. Additional Qualifications The successful candidate must specialize in American political behavior and be prepared to teach courses in quantitative methods, political behavior, and parties and elections, as well as our introductory course in American government. While ABDs will be considered, the successful candidate must have a PhD in political science by the time of initial appointment in August 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate potential for both excellent teaching and sustained scholarship published in recognized, peer-reviewed venues. They must also be willing to contribute to service activities. Link to Job Description http://www.missouristate.edu/human/jobdescriptions/21377.htm Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date (If 