    "https://jobs.missouristate.edu/postings/88789": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Early American History) - 9 month appointment",
      "description": "Missouri State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor (Early American History) - 9 month appointment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Missouri State University Office of Human Resources Part-Time Staff Positions Assistant Professor (Early American History) - 9 month appointment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The first date of consideration is October 22, 2026, with the position remaining open until filled. To apply, submit a cover letter, CV, unofficial transcripts, three confidential letters of recommendation and syllabi for the first half of the U.S. survey and an upper-level course in American History. All application material, including letters of recommendation, must be submitted electronically to https://jobs.missouristate.edu/postings/87958 . Official transcripts required at time of hire. Employment will require a criminal background check at University expense. Missouri Sate is an equal opportunity employer and institution. Questions should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Chelsea Davis at CGDavis@MissouriState.edu . Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor (Early American History) - 9 month appointment Work Location Springfield Campus Out-of-State Employment Out-of-state employment is limited to Arkansas, Virginia, Maryland, and Washington, D.C., and subject to supervisor approval. Department History HR Home Department 020613 HISTORY Pay Grade Unclassified Sponsorship Information Applicants must be currently authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States on a full-time basis. This position may not be eligible for work visa sponsorship. Position only available to current, regular, full-time Missouri State University employees? No, Position is available to all applicants. Faculty Appointment Type Tenure Track Term (if applicable) 9 month